@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Fixed physical coordinates during nuisance fitting
+
+The separate v4.1 installer `groops/extension/native_nuisance_v41.py` follows
+the corrected numerical and nuisance-performance installers. Its runtime switch
+is `ORBIT_POC_NUISANCE_FIXED_DYNAMICS=1`; absent or `0` retains the previous
+path. Other values reject. The bounded dynamic-design installer follows this
+installer and replaces the heap finiteness scan with the sealed store's
+ingestion certificate.
+
+The candidate removes two operations whose physical correction is exactly zero:
+
+- A nuisance update previously multiplied both complete trajectory design
+  matrices by a zero vector. The candidate verifies every correction value,
+  demands finite immutable-design certificates, then adds zero vectors without
+  reading the design matrices. Native clock-dependent position and velocity
+  interpolation still runs, including the mandatory zero-update replay.
+- Conditional ionosphere recovery previously interpolated every dynamic design
+  column before multiplying those columns by zero. A scoped `profile_step`
+  guard checks all physical coordinates before replacing those columns with
+  zeros. Native query/stencil/remainder validation remains active. The scope
+  ends before trial evaluation, so full weighted rows, rank certification,
+  physical proposals and covariance retain their original design values.
+
+Neither operation uses a tolerance to identify zero. A subnormal nonzero
+correction uses the ordinary product. Invalid coordinates, invalid queries,
+missing certificates and inconsistent certificate dimensions reject. Parameter
+updates still invalidate covariance. Every cold profile, zero replay,
+line-search trial, convergence threshold and objective/prior row remains.
+
+`*.nuisance_fixed_dynamics.json` records cumulative parent-process counters.
+Forked child counters are deliberately excluded; these sidecars do not claim
+to measure total saved work or certify a fit.
+
+The standalone guards and installer contracts run with
+`ORBIT_POC_V41_COMPONENT_TESTS=1 python -m pytest tests/test_nuisance_v41.py`.
+They check default behavior, source installation, exact-zero and finite-value
+guards, invalid query callbacks, scope cleanup and fork isolation. They do not
+prove complete native equivalence. Before use, run the unchanged native and
+correction suites plus actual pulse/density GNSS profiles with the switch off
+and on, including nonzero full priors, both observation accumulation modes,
+changed receiver clocks, pulse-side queries, rejected trials and covariance
+freshness. Compare full scientific artifacts and final linearizations. The
+large failed inputs remain necessary to establish whether these changes fix
+the observed timeouts.
