index 0000000..02728ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/v41-native-design-storage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Native GNSS derivative storage in v4.1
+
+The v4 density failures exposed two distinct allocations. The fixed-parameter
+closure evaluator retained full position/velocity designs, and the GNSS orbit
+parametrization retained another pair across nuisance-process forks. The v4.1
+storage adapter addresses the GNSS pair. The previously added blocked closure
+evaluator remains a separate component.
+
+`native_design_storage_v41.py` installs after `native_nuisance_v41.py`. The native
+runtime selects `ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_STORAGE=disk`; the compatibility default
+remains `memory`. Disk mode requires an explicit existing
+`ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_SCRATCH` directory. Block size is controlled by
+`ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_BLOCK_EPOCHS`, a canonical integer in `[1,4096]` with default
+64. The v4.1 run specification pins these values and the source/build/input
+hashes. None of these controls changes observations, their support, measurement
+weights, priors, parameter units, convergence thresholds or covariance authority.
+
+The adapter calls the existing `VariationalEquationFromFile::integrateArc` on
+consecutive ranges of the original native grid. One persistent native model
+retains its chronological integration accumulator throughout construction. Each
+position and velocity block contains every original dynamic parameter. Values
+are checked for finiteness, then written as the native contiguous column-major
+binary64 bytes. Computational cuts introduce no force boundaries or priors.
+
+Each design owns a preallocated, immediately unlinked regular scratch file.
+Allocation or I/O failures are fatal; there is no heap fallback. On completion,
+the sole writable descriptor is replaced by a readonly descriptor for the same
+inode, with device, inode, size and unlink state checked. Reads use `pread`, so
+forked children cannot change a shared file offset. A two-block cache is reset
+when its process identity changes. Closing the last inherited descriptor frees
+the scratch storage, including when an owned process is killed.
+Only the process that creates a store may append to or seal it. Forked children
+cannot mutate an incompletely constructed store; completed stores remain
+available for immutable reads in both parent and child.
+
+`DesignRows::row` reconstructs bounded native Matrix slices from the saved
+blocks. Existing piecewise interpolation entrypoints accept this source by a
+template parameter; their bodies, polynomial stencil selection, pulse-side
+convention, time remainders and Twofold arithmetic are unchanged. The native
+piecewise routine requests only the physical interpolation segment. A segment
+or block larger than 64 MiB is rejected explicitly. This is an implementation
+resource bound, not a change to a physical segment or interpolation stencil.
+
+Initial reference updates, subsequent dynamic updates, native Cartesian
+covariance products and observation-epoch covariance products all use bounded
+row blocks. The original parameter covariance, including marginalized nuisance
+uncertainty, is preserved. These BLAS calls have different row dimensions from
+the full-matrix path; numerical equivalence must be measured under the existing
+acceptance gates. Storage alone does not establish convergence or authorize a
+covariance.
+
+The ingestion certificate is available only for completed finite designs. The
+fixed-dynamics optimization uses this certificate before omitting products with
+an exactly zero dynamic correction. Receiver-clock-driven trajectory
+interpolation still runs, including during a zero-update replay.
+
+Each selected runtime writes `.design_storage.jsonl` diagnostic records next to
+its native QR prefix. Records identify the process and unlinked file, shape,
+block size, reserved/written/read scratch bytes, cache loads/hits and I/O wall
+time. The per-block FNV-1a checksum detects read corruption; it is not a
+cryptographic provenance hash. Source, input and executable SHA256 pins remain
+in the run manifest. Process-tree RSS accounting and its 8 GiB limit are
+unchanged, and disk storage costs remain part of elapsed time.
+
+The automated component checks use the actual selected native Matrix, BLAS and
+corrected Polynomial implementation. They cover block sizes, exact derivative
+bytes, interpolation at physical boundaries with time remainders, products,
+selected covariance, alias/fork lifetimes, descriptor cleanup, malformed state,
+truncation, corruption and allocation failure. Full native linearization,
+objective, nuisance replay, rank and fit-equivalence gates remain required;
+passing these component checks does not replace them.
diff --git a/groops/extension/designRowsV41.h b/groops/extension/designRowsV41.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..83b3da5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/groops/extension/designRowsV41.h
@@ -0,0 +1,376 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+#ifndef ORBIT_POC_DESIGN_ROWS_V41_H
+#define ORBIT_POC_DESIGN_ROWS_V41_H
+#include "base/import.h"
+#include <array>
+#include <cerrno>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <cstring>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <iomanip>
+#include <limits>
+#include <memory>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+
+// Immutable native binary64 design rows. This is storage, not a replacement
+// tangent operator: all columns and every chronological native epoch survive.
+// No mapping or Matrix allocator is changed. A cache holds at most two native
+// blocks; reads use pread so forked trials never share a mutable file offset.
+namespace OrbitPoc
+{
+namespace DesignStorage
+{
+using Clock=std::chrono::steady_clock;
+inline double seconds(Clock::time_point start)
+{return std::chrono::duration<double>(Clock::now()-start).count();}
+inline void fail(const std::string &what)
+{throw(Exception("GNSS design storage: "+what));}
+inline std::uint64_t product(std::uint64_t a,std::uint64_t b)
+{
+  if(b && a>std::uint64_t(std::numeric_limits<off_t>::max())/b)fail("byte size overflow");
+  return a*b;
+}
+inline UInt blockEpochs()
+{
+  const char *raw=std::getenv("ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_BLOCK_EPOCHS");
+  const std::string text=raw?raw:"64";UInt value=0;
+  if(text.empty() || (text.size()>1&&text.front()=='0'))fail("block epochs must be canonical 1..4096");
+  for(char c:text)
+  {
+    if(c<'0'||c>'9'||value>409||(value==409&&c>'6'))fail("block epochs must be canonical 1..4096");
+    value=10*value+UInt(c-'0');
+  }
+  if(!value)fail("block epochs must be canonical 1..4096");
+  return value;
+}
+inline bool enabled()
+{
+  const char *raw=std::getenv("ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_STORAGE");
+  const std::string text=raw?raw:"memory";
+  if(text=="memory")return false;
+  if(text=="disk"){blockEpochs();return true;}
+  fail("ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_STORAGE must be memory or disk");return false;
+}
+inline std::string directory()
+{
+  const char *raw=std::getenv("ORBIT_POC_GNSS_DESIGN_SCRATCH");
+  if(!raw||!*raw)fail("disk storage requires an explicit scratch directory");
+  return raw;
+}
+inline void finite(const_MatrixSliceRef value)
+{
+  for(UInt column=0;column<value.columns();column++)
+    for(UInt row=0;row<value.rows();row++)
+      if(!std::isfinite(value(row,column)))fail("nonfinite native derivative");
+}
+// An integrity checksum, NOT a source/provenance cryptographic hash. Exact
+// source/build/input SHA256 pins remain the responsibility of the run manifest.
+inline std::uint64_t checksum(const void *data,std::size_t bytes)
+{
+  const auto *p=static_cast<const unsigned char*>(data);
+  std::uint64_t hash=14695981039346656037ULL;
+  for(std::size_t i=0;i<bytes;i++){hash^=p[i];hash*=1099511628211ULL;}
+  return hash;
+}
+inline void io(int fd,void *buffer,std::size_t bytes,off_t offset,bool write)
+{
+  auto *data=static_cast<char*>(buffer);
+  while(bytes)
+  {
+    const ssize_t done=write ? ::pwrite(fd,data,bytes,offset) : ::pread(fd,data,bytes,offset);
+    if(done<0&&errno==EINTR)continue;
+    if(done<=0)fail(std::string(write?"write":"read")+" failed or ended early: "+(done<0?std::strerror(errno):"unexpected EOF"));
+    data+=done;bytes-=std::size_t(done);offset+=done;
+  }
+}
+struct Block {UInt first,rows;std::uint64_t offset,bytes,checksum;};
+struct Backing
+{
+  int fd=-1;UInt rows=0,columns=0,blockRows=0,writtenRows=0;
+  bool sealed=false,finiteValidated=false;
+  std::uint64_t bytes=0,writtenBytes=0;
+  dev_t device=0;ino_t inode=0;pid_t creator=::getpid();
+  double writeSeconds=0;
+  std::vector<Block> blocks;
+  Backing(UInt rowCount,UInt columnCount,UInt blockSize):rows(rowCount),columns(columnCount),blockRows(blockSize)
+  {
+    if(!rows||!columns||!blockRows)fail("empty store geometry");
+    bytes=product(product(rows,columns),sizeof(Double));
+    if(product(product(std::min(rows,blockRows),columns),sizeof(Double))>64ULL*1024*1024)
+      fail("one design block exceeds the 64 MiB storage bound");
+    const auto path=directory();
+    const int dir=::open(path.c_str(),O_RDONLY|O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC);
+    if(dir<0)fail("cannot open scratch directory: "+std::string(std::strerror(errno)));
+    // openat+O_EXCL and immediate unlink leave only owned descriptors, including
+    // on SIGKILL. No shared filename can be replaced while a trial is reading.
+    static std::uint64_t sequence=0;
+    std::string name;
+    for(unsigned attempt=0;attempt<128;attempt++)
+    {
+      name="orbit-design-"+std::to_string(::getpid())+"-"+std::to_string(++sequence);
+      fd=::openat(dir,name.c_str(),O_RDWR|O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC,0600);
+      if(fd>=0||errno!=EEXIST)break;
+    }
+    const int saved=errno;
+    if(fd<0){::close(dir);fail("cannot create owned store: "+std::string(std::strerror(saved)));}
+    if(::unlinkat(dir,name.c_str(),0)!=0)
+    {const int error=errno;::close(fd);fd=-1;::close(dir);fail("cannot unlink owned store: "+std::string(std::strerror(error)));}
+    ::close(dir);
+    try
+    {
+      struct stat state{};
+      if(::fstat(fd,&state)!=0||!S_ISREG(state.st_mode)||state.st_nlink!=0)fail("unexpected owned store identity");
+      device=state.st_dev;inode=state.st_ino;
+      // Reserve real scratch capacity before integration. ENOSPC and unsupported
+      // fallocate are explicit failures; there is no heap or sparse-file fallback.
+      const int error=::posix_fallocate(fd,0,off_t(bytes));
+      if(error)fail("cannot reserve scratch bytes: "+std::string(std::strerror(error)));
+    }
+    catch(...){::close(fd);fd=-1;throw;}
+  }
+  ~Backing(){if(fd>=0)::close(fd);}
+  Backing(const Backing&)=delete;Backing&operator=(const Backing&)=delete;
+  void append(const_MatrixSliceRef values)
+  {
+    if(::getpid()!=creator)fail("only the creating process may append an unsealed design");
+    if(sealed||writtenRows>=rows||values.rows()!=std::min(blockRows,rows-writtenRows)||values.columns()!=columns)
+      fail("append order, dimensions or sealed state mismatch");
+    finite(values);
+    Matrix packed(values); // exact native copy; contiguous column-major bytes
+    const auto start=Clock::now();
+    const auto count=product(product(packed.rows(),packed.columns()),sizeof(Double));
+    io(fd,const_cast<Double*>(packed.const_field()),std::size_t(count),off_t(writtenBytes),true);
+    blocks.push_back({writtenRows,values.rows(),writtenBytes,count,checksum(packed.const_field(),std::size_t(count))});
+    writtenRows+=values.rows();writtenBytes+=count;writeSeconds+=seconds(start);
+  }
+  void seal()
+  {
+    if(::getpid()!=creator)fail("only the creating process may seal a design");
+    if(sealed||writtenRows!=rows||writtenBytes!=bytes)fail("incomplete or repeated seal");
+    if(::fsync(fd)!=0)fail("cannot persist completed design: "+std::string(std::strerror(errno)));
+    // Replace the sole writable descriptor with a readonly descriptor of the
+    // SAME unlinked inode. All later writes are impossible through this object.
+    const std::string path="/proc/self/fd/"+std::to_string(fd);
+    const int readonly=::open(path.c_str(),O_RDONLY|O_CLOEXEC);
+    if(readonly<0)fail("cannot seal store readonly");
+    struct stat state{};
+    if(::fstat(readonly,&state)!=0||state.st_dev!=device||state.st_ino!=inode||state.st_nlink!=0||std::uint64_t(state.st_size)!=bytes)
+    {::close(readonly);fail("sealed store identity or length mismatch");}
+    ::close(fd);fd=readonly;sealed=true;finiteValidated=true;
+  }
+};
+}
+
+class DesignRows
+{
+  Matrix heap;
+  std::shared_ptr<DesignStorage::Backing> backing;
+  struct Cache {std::size_t index=std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max();Matrix value;std::uint64_t used=0;};
+  mutable std::array<Cache,2> cache;
+  mutable pid_t cacheProcess=::getpid();
+  mutable std::uint64_t sequence=0,readBytes=0,loads=0,hits=0;
+  mutable double readSeconds=0;
+  bool heapFinite=false;
+  const Matrix &load(std::size_t index)const
+  {
+    if(!backing||!backing->sealed||index>=backing->blocks.size())DesignStorage::fail("unsealed or missing read block");
+    if(cacheProcess!=::getpid())
+    {cache={};sequence=readBytes=loads=hits=0;readSeconds=0;cacheProcess=::getpid();}
+    for(auto &entry:cache)if(entry.index==index){entry.used=++sequence;hits++;return entry.value;}
+    auto &entry=cache[cache[0].used<=cache[1].used?0:1];
+    const auto &block=backing->blocks.at(index);
+    Matrix value(block.rows,columns(),Matrix::NOFILL);
+    const auto start=DesignStorage::Clock::now();
+    DesignStorage::io(backing->fd,value.field(),std::size_t(block.bytes),off_t(block.offset),false);
+    if(DesignStorage::checksum(value.const_field(),std::size_t(block.bytes))!=block.checksum)
+      DesignStorage::fail("stored native derivative integrity mismatch");
+    readSeconds+=DesignStorage::seconds(start);readBytes+=block.bytes;loads++;
+    entry.value=std::move(value);entry.index=index;entry.used=++sequence;return entry.value;
+  }
+public:
+  DesignRows()=default;
+  explicit DesignRows(const Matrix &value):heap(value){DesignStorage::finite(heap);heapFinite=true;}
+  static DesignRows disk(UInt rows,UInt columns,UInt blockRows)
+  {DesignRows value;value.backing=std::make_shared<DesignStorage::Backing>(rows,columns,blockRows);return value;}
+  UInt rows()const{return backing?backing->rows:heap.rows();}
+  UInt columns()const{return backing?backing->columns:heap.columns();}
+  bool isDisk()const{return bool(backing);}
+  bool finiteValidated()const{return backing?backing->sealed&&backing->finiteValidated:heapFinite;}
+  const Matrix &denseMatrix()const
+  {if(backing)DesignStorage::fail("dense access to disk design is forbidden");return heap;}
+  UInt blockRows()const{return backing?backing->blockRows:rows();}
+  void append(const_MatrixSliceRef value)
+  {if(!backing)DesignStorage::fail("append requires disk store");backing->append(value);}
+  void seal(){if(!backing)DesignStorage::fail("seal requires disk store");backing->seal();}
+  // Intentionally supports only the native zero-column validation view. It
+  // cannot accidentally materialize a trajectory-wide column subset.
+  Matrix column(UInt first,UInt count)const
+  {if(first||count)DesignStorage::fail("only zero-column query validation is supported");return Matrix(rows(),0);}
+  Matrix row(UInt first,UInt count=1)const
+  {
+    if(first>rows()||count>rows()-first)DesignStorage::fail("row range outside native design");
+    if(!backing)return heap.row(first,count);
+    if(!backing->sealed)DesignStorage::fail("read before immutable seal");
+    if(DesignStorage::product(DesignStorage::product(count,columns()),sizeof(Double))>64ULL*1024*1024)
+      DesignStorage::fail("requested physical interpolation segment exceeds 64 MiB; unsupported storage geometry");
+    Matrix result(count,columns(),Matrix::NOFILL);
+    for(UInt output=0;output<count;)
+    {
+      const UInt original=first+output;
+      const std::size_t index=original/backing->blockRows;
+      const auto &block=backing->blocks.at(index);
+      const UInt offset=original-block.first;
+      const UInt length=std::min(count-output,block.rows-offset);
+      copy(load(index).row(offset,length),result.row(output,length));output+=length;
+    }
+    return result;
+  }
+  Matrix operator*(const_MatrixSliceRef rhs)const
+  {
+    if(rhs.rows()!=columns())DesignStorage::fail("matrix product dimensions differ");
+    if(!backing)return heap*rhs;
+    if(DesignStorage::product(DesignStorage::product(rows(),rhs.columns()),sizeof(Double))>64ULL*1024*1024)
+      DesignStorage::fail("unbounded design product; use row blocks");
+    Matrix result(rows(),rhs.columns());
+    for(UInt first=0;first<rows();)
+    {
+      const UInt count=std::min(blockRows(),rows()-first);
+      matMult(1.,row(first,count),rhs,result.row(first,count));first+=count;
+    }
+    return result;
+  }
+  void addProduct(const_MatrixSliceRef rhs,MatrixSliceRef output)const
+  {
+    if(rhs.rows()!=columns()||output.rows()!=rows()||output.columns()!=rhs.columns())DesignStorage::fail("add-product dimensions differ");
+    if(!backing){matMult(1.,heap,rhs,output);return;}
+    for(UInt first=0;first<rows();)
+    {
+      const UInt count=std::min(blockRows(),rows()-first);
+      matMult(1.,row(first,count),rhs,output.row(first,count));first+=count;
+    }
+  }
+  void report(const char *stage)const
+  {
+    if(!backing)return;
+    const char *raw=std::getenv("ORBIT_POC_NUMERICS_QR_PREFIX");
+    if(!raw||!*raw)DesignStorage::fail("disk diagnostics require native QR output prefix");
+    std::ofstream out(std::string(raw)+".design_storage.jsonl",std::ios::app);
+    out<<std::setprecision(17)<<"{\"schema\":\"orbit-poc-design-storage-v41\",\"stage\":\""<<stage
+       <<"\",\"creator_pid\":"<<backing->creator<<",\"pid\":"<<::getpid()
+       <<",\"device\":"<<backing->device<<",\"inode\":"<<backing->inode
+       <<",\"rows\":"<<rows()<<",\"columns\":"<<columns()<<",\"block_rows\":"<<blockRows()
+       <<",\"sealed\":"<<(backing->sealed?"true":"false")<<",\"finite_validated\":"<<(finiteValidated()?"true":"false")
+       <<",\"scratch_reserved_bytes\":"<<backing->bytes<<",\"scratch_written_bytes\":"<<backing->writtenBytes
+       <<",\"write_wall_seconds\":"<<backing->writeSeconds<<",\"read_bytes\":"<<readBytes
+       <<",\"read_wall_seconds\":"<<readSeconds<<",\"block_loads\":"<<loads<<",\"cache_hits\":"<<hits
+       <<",\"checksum_kind\":\"fnv1a64_integrity_not_provenance\",\"cache_block_bound\":2}\n";
+    out.close();if(!out)DesignStorage::fail("cannot write diagnostic receipt");
+  }
+};
+
+struct StoredVariationalEquation
+{
+  std::vector<Time> times;Vector pos0,vel0;DesignRows PosDesign,VelDesign;
+};
+template<class Model> StoredVariationalEquation integrateStoredDesigns(Model &model,const std::vector<Time> &times)
+{
+  if(times.empty())DesignStorage::fail("empty native time grid");
+  StoredVariationalEquation result;
+  if(!DesignStorage::enabled())
+  {
+    auto native=model.integrateArc(times.front(),times.back(),TRUE,TRUE);
+    result.times=std::move(native.times);result.pos0=std::move(native.pos0);result.vel0=std::move(native.vel0);
+    result.PosDesign=DesignRows(native.PosDesign);result.VelDesign=DesignRows(native.VelDesign);return result;
+  }
+  const UInt block=DesignStorage::blockEpochs(),columns=model.parameterCount();
+  if(times.size()>std::numeric_limits<UInt>::max()/3)DesignStorage::fail("epoch count overflow");
+  result.times=times;result.pos0=Vector(3*times.size());result.vel0=Vector(3*times.size());
+  result.PosDesign=DesignRows::disk(3*times.size(),columns,3*block);
+  result.VelDesign=DesignRows::disk(3*times.size(),columns,3*block);
+  for(UInt first=0;first<times.size();)
+  {
+    const UInt count=std::min(block,UInt(times.size()-first));
+    // Same persistent native Alpha/integrand history, never restarted at a cut.
+    auto native=model.integrateArc(times.at(first),times.at(first+count-1),TRUE,TRUE);
+    if(model.parameterCount()!=columns||native.times.size()!=count||native.pos0.rows()!=3*count||native.vel0.rows()!=3*count)
+      DesignStorage::fail("native block geometry changed");
+    for(UInt i=0;i<count;i++)
+      if(native.times.at(i).mjdInt()!=times.at(first+i).mjdInt()||native.times.at(i).mjdMod()!=times.at(first+i).mjdMod())
+        DesignStorage::fail("native block time identity changed");
+    result.PosDesign.append(native.PosDesign);result.VelDesign.append(native.VelDesign);
+    copy(native.pos0,result.pos0.row(3*first,3*count));copy(native.vel0,result.vel0.row(3*first,3*count));first+=count;
+  }
+  result.PosDesign.seal();result.VelDesign.seal();
+  result.PosDesign.report("sealed");result.VelDesign.report("sealed");return result;
+}
+
+inline Matrix cartesianCovarianceRows(const_MatrixSliceRef position,const_MatrixSliceRef velocity,
+                                     const_MatrixSliceRef parameterCovariance)
+{
+  const UInt count=parameterCovariance.rows();
+  if(!count||parameterCovariance.columns()!=count||position.rows()%3||velocity.rows()!=position.rows()||
+     position.columns()!=count||velocity.columns()!=count)
+    DesignStorage::fail("Cartesian covariance design dimensions differ");
+  const UInt epochs=position.rows()/3;
+  const Matrix posCov=position*parameterCovariance,velCov=velocity*parameterCovariance;
+  Matrix rows(epochs,36);
+  for(UInt epoch=0;epoch<epochs;epoch++)
+  {
+    Matrix design(6,count),weighted(6,count);
+    copy(position.row(3*epoch,3),design.row(0,3));copy(velocity.row(3*epoch,3),design.row(3,3));
+    copy(posCov.row(3*epoch,3),weighted.row(0,3));copy(velCov.row(3*epoch,3),weighted.row(3,3));
+    const Matrix covariance=weighted*design.trans();
+    for(UInt i=0;i<6;i++)for(UInt j=0;j<6;j++)
+    {
+      const Double value=0.5*(covariance(i,j)+covariance(j,i));
+      if(!std::isfinite(value)||((i==j)&&(value<=0)))DesignStorage::fail("invalid native Cartesian covariance");
+      rows(epoch,6*i+j)=value;
+    }
+  }
+  return rows;
+}
+
+inline Matrix storedCartesianCovariance(const DesignRows &position,const DesignRows &velocity,
+                                       const_MatrixSliceRef parameterCovariance)
+{
+  if(position.rows()%3||position.rows()!=velocity.rows()||position.columns()!=velocity.columns()||position.isDisk()!=velocity.isDisk())
+    DesignStorage::fail("position/velocity storage covariance geometry differs");
+  if(!position.isDisk())return cartesianCovarianceRows(position.denseMatrix(),velocity.denseMatrix(),parameterCovariance);
+  Matrix result(position.rows()/3,36);
+  for(UInt first=0;first<position.rows();)
+  {
+    const UInt count=std::min(position.blockRows(),position.rows()-first);
+    const Matrix rows=cartesianCovarianceRows(position.row(first,count),velocity.row(first,count),parameterCovariance);
+    copy(rows,result.row(first/3,count/3));first+=count;
+  }
+  position.report("native_covariance");velocity.report("native_covariance");return result;
+}
+
+template<class Polynomial> Matrix storedObservationCovariance(const Polynomial &polynomial,const std::vector<Time> &queries,
+    const DesignRows &position,const DesignRows &velocity,const_MatrixSliceRef parameterCovariance)
+{
+  if(position.isDisk()!=velocity.isDisk())DesignStorage::fail("position/velocity observation storage differs");
+  if(!position.isDisk())
+  {
+    const Matrix pos=polynomial.interpolate(queries,position.denseMatrix(),3);
+    const Matrix vel=polynomial.interpolate(queries,velocity.denseMatrix(),3,TRUE);
+    return cartesianCovarianceRows(pos,vel,parameterCovariance);
+  }
+  Matrix result(queries.size(),36);
+  const UInt block=std::max(UInt(1),position.blockRows()/3);
+  for(UInt first=0;first<queries.size();)
+  {
+    const UInt count=std::min(block,UInt(queries.size()-first));
+    const std::vector<Time> part(queries.begin()+first,queries.begin()+first+count);
+    const Matrix pos=polynomial.interpolate(part,position,3);
+    const Matrix vel=polynomial.interpolate(part,velocity,3,TRUE);
+    const Matrix rows=cartesianCovarianceRows(pos,vel,parameterCovariance);
+    copy(rows,result.row(first,count));first+=count;
+  }
+  position.report("observation_covariance");velocity.report("observation_covariance");return result;
+}
+}
+#endif
